            <div xml:id="d674">

                <pb facs="0970" n="864" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg864"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">702.6111/313: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-09T14:00:00-05:00">December 9, 1939—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>272. Your 774, October 19, 3 p.m. The Soviet Ambassador in complaining with
                    regard to the examination by the United States Customs authorities of the
                    effects of Zaikine has asked whether the Soviet customs
                    authorities examine the baggage of American consular officers assigned to Moscow
                    who are in possession of diplomatic passports. Please cite several
                    instances.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
